   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«o», «a», «os», «as»",
     "texto": [
      "In a positive main clause, the object pronoun usually goes **after** the verb, joined with a hyphen: **Vi o filme** → **Vi-o** (I saw it), **Comprei-a** (I bought it).",
      "This is an initial rule for European Portuguese; the position also depends on the type of clause and the words that introduce it."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "When it comes first",
     "texto": [
      "In common contexts such as after **não**, **nunca** or **que**, the pronoun goes before the verb and without a hyphen: **Não o vi**, **Nunca a comprei**, **Disse que o viu**.",
      "**Também o vi** (I also saw it) is another common example. Don't take a single rule as the rule for every sentence."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Pronoun position",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "Affirmative sentence (verb first)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Comprei-a ontem.",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
